{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara","id":547609,"title":"Beast: Makara","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-09T15:48:36-07:00","id":547609,"title":"Beast: Makara","content":"As much as I love me some Lovecraftian Dagon/Deep One/Kraken sea monster awesomeness, I'm not quite feeling where Makara can fit outside of a watery themed character. I see the Giants as those who feared powerlessness, the Lurkers are those who feared hunters in their dark dreams who do what their title says, Namtaru is the fear of revulsion or being revolting to others, of creepy-crawlies etc and Ugallu is the fear of exposure (literal and secrets of theirs being exposed)...<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where the Makara fit in outside of a fear of drowning... I thought about the drowning perhaps being someone fearing drowning in problems thrown their way, though I thought the Giants fear of power being taken covered that. I know the fear of water is a legitimate thing, though I'm struggling to link such a Beast who had this nightmare into a character concept.<br /> <br /> I love the Ugallu and I can think of concepts for all the Beast Families, though all I can think of for a Makara is someone who feared being swallowed up and drowned by their life, though that could easily be a Giant, personified into a Eshmaki or others.<br /> <br /> Long story short, I'm not really grokking the Makara compared to the others... Can anyone tell me how they may have their recurring Nightmare before Homecoming and not have it linked to literal water phobia?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:53:20-07:00","id":547624,"title":"","content":"They Also Represent Fear of the &quot;Deep&quot; Deep could also be underground. From that it's not that far too come up with something like.. say a Graboid from Tremors...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:57:50-07:00","id":547630,"title":"","content":"Makara, I believe, aren't just the fear of drowning, but the fear of that which has been drowned(literally or metaphorically). Ancient secrets and forgotten lore, things man was not meant to know and civilizations best lost, these are the things which lurk within the nightmares the Leviathans call home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Added clarification 06-09-2015, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T15:59:31-07:00","id":547631,"title":"","content":"Tying into Zeal, it's also fear of repressed emotions.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm planning anything with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:02:55-07:00","id":547633,"title":"","content":"I would imagine being overwhelmed fits into their portfolio as well. Not in the capacity where a giant is just overwhelmingly powerful or something more on the grounds of there just being too much, too many problems, too many possibilities, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:06:46-07:00","id":547639,"title":"","content":"The Makara are the fear of the depths, the fear of the things that swim beneath the waves and all those tipically lovecraftian things like civilizations, ancestors and knowledge drowned by history - perhaps for the best. They are the the fear of horrible heritages (wink wink), repressed memories, emotions and secrets you nope never to see resurface.<br /> <br /> Basically, aside from the obvious drowning, acquatic beasts and immensity of the ocean compared to a puny human fears, they also represent the fear of terrible things returning afloat to torment you, either ones from your past or those coming from even more distant times upon which you have no knowledge or control whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=547633#post547633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would imagine being overwhelmed fits into their portfolio as well. Not in the capacity where a giant is just overwhelmingly powerful or something more on the grounds of there just being too much, too many problems, too many possibilities, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This too. Excellent point","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-09-2015, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:11:16-07:00","id":547642,"title":"","content":"Makara are more than the fear of drowning: they're the fear of the DEPHTS, which include the fear of what lies beneath, that things aren't what they appear to be, that a seemily good thing hides a terrible danger.<br /> They're the monsters who lure you in ther lairs with seet words, coy smiles and honeyed promises only to reveal grasping limbs and rows of sharp teeth once you're in too deep.<br /> <br /> They're the pretty gold diggers with a shark-like divorce attorney on speed dial, the Sirens serenading doomed sailors, and the Megalodons escaping some forgotten abyss to plague the seas once more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T16:37:21-07:00","id":547691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=547624#post547624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They Also Represent Fear of the &amp;quot;Deep&amp;quot; Deep could also be underground. From that it's not that far too come up with something like.. say a Graboid from Tremors...</div> </div> </div> </div>I suddenly want to play a graboid now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T18:38:32-07:00","id":547853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=547631#post547631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tying into Zeal, it's also fear of repressed emotions.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm planning anything with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I like. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I know it seems quite a few are talking about the fear of cosmic horror and unknown maddening knowledge, but wouldn't things hidden tie in with the Eshmaki instead, or is that a fear of the more personified monster/boogeyman under the bed for that one?<br /> <br /> I'm going to need an example of a recurring Nightmare for Makara that involves some kind of hidden knowledge, ancient lore, etc. As said before in my OP, I think being overwhelmed is an Anakim thing as I'd link it with losing power, or control of one's life.<br /> <br /> I <i>do</i> like the idea of a secret and a Nightmare recurring of the proto-Beast not wanting it to get out, though I think that would come under exposure and be an Ugallu thing. I kind of think perhaps I'm getting more an idea for where to place the Makara with reading your posts though... The Nightmare of being inconsequential <i>in the end</i> (rather than making someone feel small there and then as an Anakim Homecoming may do) to the greater Universe as a whole, being little more than a speck of dust in the vastness of space, I think that could make a good Makara Homecoming Nightmare.<br /> <br /> I guess also that an Anakim intimidates from the off, the Ugallu wishes to expose, the Eshmaki lurks in the dark, Namtaru are the squick and then Makara lure in before showing the mind-bending horror, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:31:07-07:00","id":547934,"title":"","content":"Makara can also be about other things.<br /> <br /> Being pulled away from the familiar by strong currents until you are too far out to swim home. Being trapped in a claustrophobic space (you are buried alive! You are in a van that just went off a bridge and is now sitting on the bottom of the river and slowly filling with water! You are crawling through a cave but it just keeps getting smaller and smaller and oh god you're stuck!) also fit into their wheelhouse. <br /> <br /> It's not always about the water. It's about what the water represents: being out of your element. Water is scary because you can't breathe and everything else swims faster than you and you can't hear very well and it requires constant exertion simply to stay where you are. Similarly hostile environments (outer space, frozen tundras, deserts, deep caves, etc) can induce terrors that could inspire unusual Makara. It's not the fear of powerlessness or helplessness, it's the fear of finding yourself in an alien world whose workings you don't understand and which is indifferent or actively hostile to your well being. Hell, you could play a Makara that embodies the nightmare of mean-girls style high school social bullshit who preys on freshmen and it would fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T20:49:04-07:00","id":547947,"title":"","content":"I actually realized that Cthulhu isn't a Makara but a mummy: priest of the old ones, phenomenally powerful, sleeps a lot, has Cult(s).<br /> <br /> In response, I resolved to make a desert-based Makara inspired by either graboids or the Sarlacc pit. Really throw some players for a loop when they go into its &quot;tomb&quot; and find a Beast instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T00:50:02-07:00","id":548142,"title":"","content":"Thanks Guru, that really helped. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also damn, BDH, that'd be fairly interesting... You could give the Beast a Kinship Nightmare from a Mummy too, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:33:53-07:00","id":548156,"title":"","content":"I may not like Beast, but my immediate character concept upon reading the preview text was a Makara with Mummy Kinship. Rather than the ocean, he has ties to the crushing weight of history, of one's isolation in the face of the ceaseless forward march of history and the inevitable decay of all great things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:44:45-07:00","id":548160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=548156#post548156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may not like Beast, but my immediate character concept upon reading the preview text was a Makara with Mummy Kinship. Rather than the ocean, he has ties to the crushing weight of history, of one's isolation in the face of the ceaseless forward march of history and the inevitable decay of all great things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Drowning under the crushing pressure of the Sands of Time? Or asphyxiating under the literal sands beneath which the Mummies are housed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T02:18:04-07:00","id":548173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=547853#post547853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know it seems quite a few are talking about the fear of cosmic horror and unknown maddening knowledge, but wouldn't things hidden tie in with the Eshmaki instead, or is that a fear of the more personified monster/boogeyman under the bed for that one?</div> </div> </div> </div>This depends.... If the Knowledge is <b>Buried</b> or <b>Hidden.</b><br /> Buried would imply it's been left in plain sight just time or nature has covered it up.<br /> Hidden would be that someone or something wants it gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T03:03:29-07:00","id":548192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=547853#post547853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to need an example of a recurring Nightmare for Makara that involves some kind of hidden knowledge, ancient lore, etc. As said before in my OP, I think being overwhelmed is an Anakim thing as I'd link it with losing power, or control of one's life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a recurring nightmare back in my childhood which can revolve around this idea : I'm trap in a building, always different, but without any mean to exit. And I know that below, somewhere, there is something infinitely evil and frightening. I know it's here, and I struggle to don't go near it, but whatever the path I'm lead to a door, the exact same door in every occurence of the nightmare, and I know behind the Thing is waiting for me. I enter throw the door and i see the horror, and I wake up out of fear, but the thing is even today I can't describe this monster. I know it has the same shape, the same nature, but in each dream the memory I wake up with is different. I remember it as a mess of strings, a pile of sheets or metallic edges, but I know it newer was any of this, just the closest form I can identify it with.<br /> <br /> And now that I remember all this stuff, the fact that the door which lead to the monster was the only fixed element of the nightmare make me wonder if I haven't an hidden trauma behind all this stuff....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T03:43:08-07:00","id":548231,"title":"","content":"I think in the 'traditional' Makara narrative there's an element of that which is safe suddenly not being so. Water gives you life, you literally cannot exist without it, but even the most placid seeming lakes is teeming with things unseen. One day you'll look down the well and see something staring back at you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T09:04:20-07:00","id":548765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=548231#post548231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in the 'traditional' Makara narrative there's an element of that which is safe suddenly not being so. Water gives you life, you literally cannot exist without it, but even the most placid seeming lakes is teeming with things unseen. One day you'll look down the well and see something staring back at you.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: sirens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T12:54:44-07:00","id":549193,"title":"","content":"The way I've been looking at it, is thinking about why people are afraid of going out into the water. One conclusion I've come to, is that it is symbolic of knowing that you are going somewhere that is dangerous to you, and risking it anyway. Before people became industrialized, it wasn't a common thing to know how to swim, even among sailors. Generally, if you fell in deep water, you were dead. <br /> <br /> To me, fear of the water is the same as the fear of taking a chance, and failing. It's the plunging feeling when you are playing a game and you need to roll anything over a 5 and the die stops on 4. It's the sinking feeling you get when you have big money riding on the Superbowl, and your star quarterback gets injured in the first quarter. It's when you think &quot;I'll be fine as long as [x] doesn't happen,&quot; right before [x] happens in a big way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T22:23:21-07:00","id":557908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arabidopsis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=548192#post548192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a recurring nightmare back in my childhood which can revolve around this idea : I'm trap in a building, always different, but without any mean to exit. And I know that below, somewhere, there is something infinitely evil and frightening. I know it's here, and I struggle to don't go near it, but whatever the path I'm lead to a door, the exact same door in every occurence of the nightmare, and I know behind the Thing is waiting for me. I enter throw the door and i see the horror, and I wake up out of fear, but the thing is even today I can't describe this monster. I know it has the same shape, the same nature, but in each dream the memory I wake up with is different. I remember it as a mess of strings, a pile of sheets or metallic edges, but I know it newer was any of this, just the closest form I can identify it with.<br /> <br /> And now that I remember all this stuff, the fact that the door which lead to the monster was the only fixed element of the nightmare make me wonder if I haven't an hidden trauma behind all this stuff....</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds a bit more like an Eshmaki Nightmare to me. Personally, I rarely remember anything of my dreams, but I <i>do</i> have a profound fear that there is something lurking in the dark, something I was not meant to see. I sometimes wonder, is it in the dark in order to hide, <b>or because the light is afraid to touch it... </b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T02:21:36-07:00","id":558031,"title":"","content":"I really want my Makara to be a twist on a Kelpie, because if I'm going to be a Beast why not be a hellish half-drowned devil horse <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T05:37:51-07:00","id":558119,"title":"","content":"Well, first, let me say that I'm deeply surprised this hasn't come up at all. I'm personally not thinking about these Families in terms of abstract fears, but what kinds of monsters they represent. The Makara represent more than just the Old Ones and the kraken. First, we have the sirens. Just look at the Atavisms that we start with the the Makara - two of the four are based on having seductive/social powers (Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song). The only two social Atavisms in the game so far. This lends us to start thinking about things like &quot;emotions deep as the ocean,&quot; &quot;drown in passion,&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> Then, the Makara are designed to be master grapplers, based on the tentacle atavism and the innate Birthright. <a href=\"http://dnd.rm-o.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/roper_scary.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">That means we're talking about monsters like the roper</a>. We could also do something like a sticky slime monster using psuedopods to move and grab things. Or just a <br /> <br /> When it comes to water, only the Heart of the Ocean atavism deals with ocean. There's also the potential of a Flooded/Suffocating lair, but those are only suggestions, not even an affinity. <br /> <br /> So, as you can see, its very easy to create a couple different Makara monsters that have nothing to do with the water. All Makara are somehow good grapplers, and many of them have a seductive edge to them. If we put them together while ignoring the water aspects? I can see something like <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=Alraune&amp;espv=2&amp;biw=1600&amp;bih=775&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CAYQ_AUoAWoVChMIq8urut2WxgIVSJINCh2JbQA_\" target=\"_blank\">the Alruane</a> as a Makara, or perhaps something based on a monster with multiple arms, like the <a href=\"http://www.greekmythology.com/images/mythology/hecatoncheires_102.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">hundred handed from Greek mythology</a>. <br /> <br /> Lots of potential here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T15:56:51-07:00","id":558812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=558119#post558119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, first, let me say that I'm deeply surprised this hasn't come up at all. I'm personally not thinking about these Families in terms of abstract fears, but what kinds of monsters they represent. The Makara represent more than just the Old Ones and the kraken. First, we have the sirens. Just look at the Atavisms that we start with the the Makara - two of the four are based on having seductive/social powers (Alien Allure and Siren's Treacherous Song). The only two social Atavisms in the game so far. This lends us to start thinking about things like &quot;emotions deep as the ocean,&quot; &quot;drown in passion,&quot; or something similar.<br /> <br /> Then, the Makara are designed to be master grapplers, based on the tentacle atavism and the innate Birthright. <a href=\"http://dnd.rm-o.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/02/roper_scary.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">That means we're talking about monsters like the roper</a>. We could also do something like a sticky slime monster using psuedopods to move and grab things. Or just a<br /> <br /> When it comes to water, only the Heart of the Ocean atavism deals with ocean. There's also the potential of a Flooded/Suffocating lair, but those are only suggestions, not even an affinity.<br /> <br /> So, as you can see, its very easy to create a couple different Makara monsters that have nothing to do with the water. All Makara are somehow good grapplers, and many of them have a seductive edge to them. If we put them together while ignoring the water aspects? I can see something like <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=Alraune&amp;espv=2&amp;biw=1600&amp;bih=775&amp;source=lnms&amp;tbm=isch&amp;sa=X&amp;ved=0CAYQ_AUoAWoVChMIq8urut2WxgIVSJINCh2JbQA_\" target=\"_blank\">the Alruane</a> as a Makara, or perhaps something based on a monster with multiple arms, like the <a href=\"http://www.greekmythology.com/images/mythology/hecatoncheires_102.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">hundred handed from Greek mythology</a>.<br /> <br /> Lots of potential here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be pedantic, but weren't the Hundred-Handed well,<span style=\"font-size:72px\"><b>GIANTS?</b></span> Pretty sure that would make them Anakim. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is 