yle=\"font-size:72px\"><b>GIANTS?</b></span> Pretty sure that would make them Anakim. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree hekatonkheires probably don't fit in with the Makara giant is not necessarily a qualifier for Anakim. I mean Jormugandr the world serpent is obviously Makara and that's a serpent so large it wraps around the entire planet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T18:50:24-07:00","id":558947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/547609-beast-makara?p=558812#post558812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to be pedantic, but weren't the Hundred-Handed well,<b>GIANTS?</b> Pretty sure that would make them Anakim. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> That depends entirely on what you're going for. In this case, I was just tossing the idea that you're a many-armed monster out there, as if a crazy pandoran monster out of promethean, not that you had to faithfully recreate the greek myth. Plus, who ever said that you had to have only one Family per monster type? Dragons can fit under Raptors or Lurker. depending on how you want to see it. <br />","signature":"","e